  "decision": "For an idle, dedicated RX 7900 XTX, recommend 114,688 total context tokens as the explicit Qwen3.8-27B pure-INT8 maximum when max-active-requests=1, AR is used, and prefix cache/MTP are off. Four different pinned ShareGPT-derived 114,683-token prompts completed consecutively with exact generated-ID accounting, zero leaked ownership, 23.322876 GiB peak, and 0.661499 GiB headroom; this supersedes the earlier conservative 96K recommendation for that exact dedicated-c1 operating contract. Keep 96K as an optional extra-margin setting. Do not transfer 112K to c>1: the current packed short-context path adds a BF16 mirror and is not an efficient INT8 capacity route. Measured 512-MiB-headroom settings are 4K/request at physical c2 and 1,280/request at physical c4; offered c8 is two c4 queue waves, not eight simultaneously resident requests.",
